{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1cef 2615 PS2 LLM-Review-1 BLOCK (3 correctness findings) → FIXED IN SCOPE with RED-first held-out tests (PS3): (255) dropped _ledger_cap magic branch; outer ledger.reserve now uses cap_usd + reserve_usd=0.0 so ANY cap nets to the whole cap (old code trapped every non-25 cap at negative remaining). (327) _ProductionAttempter.run now maps summary.incomplete → new AttemptOutcome.INCOMPLETE (transient outage; counter unchanged, no admit/quarantine) instead of misclassifying as FAILED_REPRODUCE. (444) _drift_reason now prefers an UNMINABLE_DRIFT_REASONS entry over first-match so un-minable outranks non-reproducing. 3 new held-out tests proven RED against stashed old heal.py ('failed-reproduce' vs 'unminable' etc.), GREEN after fix. Full oracle 13/13, lint+typecheck green. Amended, pushed PS3. DEFER (Phase-5 follow-up): advisories l123 cwd fallback, l135 CLI LLMError path untested, l167 counter-drop test gap."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788507769576457001,"uuid":"63c60687-73d8-489b-ba73-160a52b2a311"}